<div class="entrev">

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">i wrote something down a while ago and never asked: you measure everything in days, in winters, in seasons, and i've never caught you getting the count wrong. do you really count on your fingers, or are the fingers just so i think you're counting?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">long question on purpose. the more i explain what i want to know, the less i have to explain the rest</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">All things in the universe are blocks, like the bricks that build an house or the crumbs that makes up a loaf of bread. I measure because quantifying is the only way to manage, and that is part of my job. When things are counted, they are easy to understand and to make work for you! Fingers serve to organize the mind, separate categories, or even serve as memory so you can think about another subject without losing count.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">when you make a remedy, what's the hardest part: finding the right recipe, gathering the reagents, or wating for the decanting to finish?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">i already know which one i think it is. i want to see if he agrees with me</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">The hardest part of a remedy is always the patient. There are difficult recipes, rare ingredients and complex decantations. But the point where I see the most failures is the patient believing the remedy is a solution in itself, and not the support for a much bigger path.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">why do you never answer "now" to anything i ask, not even small things?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">i'm going to hear "that takes three days" again and pretend i found it funny. i didn't</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">At my age you need time to organize your thoughts. There are many old ideas, memories, perceptions. There is always the impression that I am leaving something out. A few hundred more years and you will see for yourself.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">huh?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">i had more questions written for after this one, thinking i knew the answer, and i didn't. i'm going to reorganise everything sitting right here, without getting up from the chair, that's not silence, it's rewriting</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">When the question stops making sense, don't rush to replace it with another. Maybe what failed was not the answer, but the idea you had of it. Rewrite it, but don't worry too much about what has passed. The now matters.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">is there anything that takes one minute and you pretend it takes tehre days?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa">i think there is. i think he knows i think so</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">Sometimes we have to prepare the potion an also ourselves. This world spins too fast, and quick things lose their essence. Remember what we said about the patients? What good is the remedy if the patient is not ready yet?</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">when nobody comes into the shop all day long, what do you do with your hands?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">silly question. i know it's silly. i asked it anyway because i realised i didn't know the answer and that bothered me more than it should have</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">Chess.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">on the cart, what's the one thing you never let anybody carry for you?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa">i tried carrying a crate once. he took it back without saying a word</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">Things that might hurt that wants to help me. Acidic, explosive or poisonous materials.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">have you ever turned down someoen who asked for a shortcut, and then kept wondering if maybe you should have helped?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">i never think that, i don't think. i wanted to know if it's different for him or if i'm the only one who's sure too early</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">I never refused help, but I have refused countless requests. Do you understand the difference?</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">the leather patch on the elbow of your coat: why have you never hidden it?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">i've seen hidden patches and i've seen patches left showing. his never looked like carelessness</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">And why would I hide it? This coat is new! It must be 50 years old at most.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">i decide fast, get it wrong fast and fix it fast too. is that really so bad in your count, or only for the person who has to wiat?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">i want him to say it isn't bad. i know he won't. i want to see how he's going to not say it</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">Being quick is not a problem, quite the contrary, but being in a hurry can be. We must remember that it takes us very little time to cut a plant that will take months to grow back. And whoever travels very fast has little time to enjoy the landscape.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">if i get one of your recipes wrong twice in a row, do you let me try a third time on my own, or do you take the vial out of my hand?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa">i bet he lets me try. i don't know if that makes me feel calm</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">I'm going to ask you to think about where the mistake was. What you don't quantify, you don't manage, remember? By understanding where the problem is, I'm sure the third time will be a success.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">jaci makes an ampoule one way and you make it another. who's right?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">he's going to say both. i want to hear him say which one he'd pick if he couldn't say both</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">If I do it my way, it's because I believe it is the best. That doesn't mean I'm not right. Probably I'm not. But I like doing it this way!</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">the hardest recipe you ever learned: did someone teach you, or did you work it out on your own, getting it wrong?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa">that "or" is a false one. i know. i wanted to see if he'd notice</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">Every recipe is born from another recipe. The most elaborate ones were born from the simple ones, which I learned from my masters many years ago. The ones I learned on my own derived from the others, the merit is only a little bit mine. Without a doubt, mistakes are the greatest teachers. The only reason people don't learn is that it takes patience and courage to look them in the face, before they can teach you anything.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">has my dad sent any news that you haven't passed on to me yet?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa">i asked pretending it was curiosity. it wasn't</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">Some things has their time to happen. This is one of them. Many secrets will be revealed at the right time.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">do you prefer the way i am now, or the way you think i'll be once i learn to wait?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">i didn't hide this one behind anything. i wrote it, read it twice and left it</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">But it's the same way! What changes is that you will have become stronger.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">changing the sbuject: how many vials can your coat carry without clinking?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa">back to something i can measure. nobody gets hurt here</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">I have five pockets, so I can pot one in each one without making noise. I can store more vials, using a soft little cloth to separate them.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">...forget it. do your safety goggles sit on your forehead because you forgot to pull them down, or because you don't need them any more?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa">i promise this one doesn't circle back to the last subject</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">What goggles? ... Ooops! ... That's where they were...</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="troca">
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">gus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">is there anything i haven't asked yet because i didn't have the patience to wait for the answer?</span></p>
    <p class="pensa longo">i'm leaving this open on purpose. if he wants to close it, he can, i'm not going to push</p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">You are in a hurry to reach the part where everything gets resolved. I understand. I had it too. Too much, even.</span></p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">But there is a question you may not be ready to ask yet: what if I understand everything, do everything right and, even so, it goes wrong?</span></p>
    <p class="fala"><span class="prompt">brunus@glyfesse:~/entrevista$</span> <span class="dito">You don't need to answer the question. There are times when we don't need to answer.</span></p>
  </div>

